---
import Layout from "../../../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout title="båzu frisør · UX Case Study">
    <link slot="head" rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com" />
    <link
        slot="head"
        rel="preconnect"
        href="https://fonts.gstatic.com"
        crossorigin
    />
    <link
        slot="head"
        href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Noto+Sans+JP:wght@300;400;500;700&family=Recia:wght@400;500;600;700&family=Space+Grotesk:wght@400;500;600;700&display=swap"
        rel="stylesheet"
    />
    <article class="bazu-case-study">
        <section class="case-study-hero">
            <div class="hero-copy">
                <p class="eyebrow">båzu frisør</p>
                <h1>A UI/UX case study for a buzz cut salon.</h1>
                <p class="lead">
                    båzu comes from bozu, the Japanese word for a shaved head or
                    buzz cut. This is a one page website concept for a fictional
                    short hair specialty salon in Oslo.
                </p>
            </div>

            <figure class="hero-media">
                <img
                    src="/img/case-studies/hero2.png"
                    alt="båzu frisør website hero screen with a buzz cut model and booking buttons"
                />
                <figcaption>
                    Current landing page direction for the concept in progress.
                </figcaption>
            </figure>

            <dl class="case-study-meta">
                <div class="meta-row">
                    <dt>Type</dt>
                    <dd>Website concept · One page</dd>
                </div>
                <div class="meta-row">
                    <dt>Year</dt>
                    <dd>2026</dd>
                </div>
                <div class="meta-row">
                    <dt>Role</dt>
                    <dd>UX design, UI design, copy, branding, planning</dd>
                </div>
                <div class="meta-row">
                    <dt>Tools</dt>
                    <dd>
                        Figma Make, Midjourney, Astro, Claude (AI assistant)
                    </dd>
                </div>
                <div class="meta-row">
                    <dt>Languages</dt>
                    <dd>Norwegian / English / Japanese</dd>
                </div>
                <div class="meta-row">
                    <dt>Status</dt>
                    <dd>Concept project</dd>
                </div>
            </dl>
        </section>

        <section class="case-study-snapshot" aria-label="Case study snapshot">
            <div>
                <span>Problem</span>
                <p>
                    Hair length is usually sold as numbers, but users need a
                    visual sense of what 1mm, 5mm, or 20mm will feel like.
                </p>
            </div>
            <div>
                <span>Approach</span>
                <p>
                    Turn the decision into a guided flow: preview the length,
                    answer a short quiz, then book with more certainty.
                </p>
            </div>
            <div>
                <span>Focus</span>
                <p>
                    A calm one page concept with a slider, five question quiz,
                    multilingual framing, and a precise salon brand direction.
                </p>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section class="case-study-overview">
            <h2>UX Strategy</h2>

            <div class="overview-item">
                <span class="overview-number">1</span>
                <div>
                    <p class="overview-title">Show less, say more.</p>
                    <p>
                        Build the trust of a specialty salon through subtraction
                        with a bold, minimal, refined expression.
                    </p>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="overview-item">
                <span class="overview-number">2</span>
                <div>
                    <p class="overview-title">
                        Guide the undecided in five questions.
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        A light quiz that answers the unspoken “which length
                        actually suits me?”
                    </p>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="overview-item">
                <span class="overview-number">3</span>
                <div>
                    <p class="overview-title">
                        See the difference before you choose.
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        A slider that previews every millimeter, so the decision
                        happens with your eyes, not your guesses.
                    </p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section class="case-study-challenge">
            <h2>The Challenge</h2>
            <p>
                The biggest fear before a buzz cut is realizing it's shorter
                than you imagined. Hair doesn't grow back the same day, and yet
                most salons reduce the choice to numbers like "3mm" and "5mm,"
                with no way to picture how it'll land on your own head.
            </p>
            <p>
                The second challenge is gender. Buzz cuts have long been coded
                as masculine, and most salon spaces and advertising follow suit.
                The reality is that people of every gender choose to cut their
                hair this short, but the existing market doesn't acknowledge
                them.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section class="case-study-user">
            <h2>The User</h2>
            <p>
                <strong>båzu frisør</strong> is designed for three overlapping groups:
            </p>
            <ul>
                <li>
                    <strong>First timers</strong> afraid of going too short
                </li>
                <li>
                    <strong>Returning short hair wearers</strong> looking to try a
                    new length
                </li>
                <li>
                    <strong>Fashion driven choosers</strong> searching for the shape
                    that suits their head
                </li>
            </ul>
            <p>
                What they share is one quiet question: <strong
                    >"Can I see it before I commit?"</strong
                > The site is built to answer that, regardless of gender, age, or
                experience.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section class="case-study-feature">
            <h2>The Slider</h2>
            <div class="feature-grid">
                <div>
                    <p class="feature-eyebrow">
                        See every millimeter, with your eyes.
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        Seven steps from 1mm to 20mm. As the slider moves, the
                        portrait crossfades to show the cut at that length, so
                        the choice is visual, not numerical.
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        I considered finer increments like 6mm and 7mm, but kept
                        it to lengths the eye can actually tell apart. Fewer
                        choices, easier decision.
                    </p>
                </div>
                <img
                    src="/img/case-studies/bazu-slider.png"
                    alt="Slider interface showing hair length preview from 1mm to 20mm"
                    class="feature-image"
                />
            </div>
        </section>

        <section class="case-study-feature">
            <h2>The Quiz</h2>
            <div class="feature-grid feature-grid--reverse">
                <img
                    src="/img/case-studies/bazu-quiz.png"
                    alt="Quiz interface: five questions for finding your ideal buzz cut length"
                    class="feature-image"
                />
                <div>
                    <p class="feature-eyebrow">
                        Five questions for the undecided.
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        Five questions across motivation, experience, head
                        shape, styling habits, and formality. The answers map to
                        a recommended length between 1mm and 20mm.
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        I avoided abstract questions like "what's your style?"
                        in favor of grounded ones like "how often do you need to
                        look formal?" The result should connect to the user's
                        actual life, not a vague aesthetic.
                    </p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section class="case-study-feature">
            <h2>The Machine</h2>
            <div class="feature-grid">
                <div>
                    <p class="feature-eyebrow">
                        Milli 0.1, precision at a tenth of a millimeter.
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        Most clippers cut in 1mm steps. Milli 0.1 cuts in 0.1mm
                        steps, guided by a 3D scan of the head. Made in Japan,
                        built where traditional Kyoto craftsmanship meets modern
                        engineering.
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        Showing the machine makes the promise tangible. It gives
                        the service a technical reason to trust it, so precision
                        feels less like a claim and more like something the user
                        can see.
                    </p>
                </div>
                <div class="machine-visual">
                    <img
                        src="/img/case-studies/milli0.1-clean.png"
                        alt="Milli 0.1: a precision clipper device with black finish and blue accents"
                        class="feature-image feature-image--machine"
                    />
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section class="case-study-visual">
            <h2>Visual Direction</h2>
            <div class="visual-grid">
                <div class="visual-copy">
                    <p class="visual-kicker">Bold · Minimal · Refined.</p>
                    <p class="visual-lead">
                        For a buzz cut, I chose earth colors close to the body:
                        skin, soil, and sand. The mint adds the playful side of
                        båzu, a small surprise that keeps simplicity from
                        feeling heavy.
                    </p>
                    <p class="visual-reference">
                        References: Aesop · Margiela · MUJI
                    </p>
                    <div class="palette-grid">
                        <div class="palette-item">
                            <span
                                class="palette-chip"
                                style="background-color: #F8F4E1;"></span>
                            <strong>Cream</strong>
                            <span>#F8F4E1</span>
                        </div>
                        <div class="palette-item">
                            <span
                                class="palette-chip"
                                style="background-color: #4E3620;"></span>
                            <strong>Earth brown</strong>
                            <span>#4E3620</span>
                        </div>
                        <div class="palette-item">
                            <span
                                class="palette-chip"
                                style="background-color: #897853;"></span>
                            <strong>Sand</strong>
                            <span>#897853</span>
                        </div>
                        <div class="palette-item">
                            <span
                                class="palette-chip"
                                style="background-color: #C8EED9;"></span>
                            <strong>Mint</strong>
                            <span>#C8EED9</span>
                        </div>
                        <div class="palette-item">
                            <span
                                class="palette-chip"
                                style="background-color: #C8963A;"></span>
                            <strong>Mustard</strong>
                            <span>#C8963A</span>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="type-panel">
                    <p class="visual-kicker">Type</p>
                    <div class="type-specimen-list">
                        <div class="type-spec type-spec--display">
                            <span class="type-role">Display</span>
                            <span class="type-name">Recia</span>
                            <p class="type-sample">
                                Even one millimeter changes you.
                            </p>
                        </div>
                        <div class="type-spec type-spec--functional">
                            <span class="type-role">Functional</span>
                            <span class="type-name">Space Grotesk</span>
                            <p class="type-sample">
                                Find your length before you book.
                            </p>
                        </div>
                        <div class="type-spec type-spec--japanese">
                            <span class="type-role">Japanese</span>
                            <span class="type-name">Noto Sans JP Light</span>
                            <p class="type-sample" lang="ja">
                                一ミリで印象は変わる。
                            </p>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section class="case-study-outcome">
            <h2>Current Direction</h2>
            <div class="outcome-gallery">
                <img
                    src="/img/case-studies/Screenshot 2026-05-24 at 22.59.20.png"
                    alt="Full webpage screen for båzu frisør"
                />
                <img
                    src="/img/case-studies/Screenshot 2026-05-24 at 22.59.32.png"
                    alt="båzu frisør website section showing the Milli 0.1 machine"
                />
                <img
                    src="/img/case-studies/Screenshot 2026-05-24 at 22.59.43.png"
                    alt="båzu frisør website booking section"
                />
            </div>
            <p>
                The concept treats the website as a decision tool, not just a
                salon brochure. Each section answers one moment of doubt: what
                the length looks like, which option fits the user, why the
                service is precise, and how to book.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section class="case-study-learned">
            <h2>What I Learned</h2>
            <p>
                The thing I underestimated was how many decisions design is
                actually made of. Color, type, the number of questions, the
                exact word in a piece of copy. Each one tests both your instinct
                for users and your own taste.
            </p>
            <p>
                I aimed for something that feels good for both sides, the person
                using it, and the person making it. Next time, I'd factor in
                technical constraints earlier, especially the difficulty of
                keeping a single portrait consistent across seven hair lengths.
            </p>
        </section>
    </article>
</Layout>

<style>
    :global(body.dark),
    :global(body:not(.dark)) {
        background: #f5f1e8;
        color: #1d1a17;
    }

    :global(body:not(.dark)::before) {
        display: none;
    }

    .bazu-case-study {
        max-width: 1040px;
        margin: 0 auto;
        padding: 5.5rem 1.5rem 7rem;
        font-family: "Space Grotesk", system-ui, sans-serif;
        color: #1d1a17;
    }

    .case-study-hero {
        display: grid;
        gap: clamp(2.4rem, 5vw, 4.5rem);
    }

    .hero-copy {
        max-width: 860px;
        padding-top: clamp(1rem, 4vw, 3rem);
    }

    .hero-media {
        margin: 0;
    }

    .hero-media img {
        display: block;
        width: 100%;
        border: 1px solid rgba(78, 54, 32, 0.12);
        border-radius: 1rem;
        box-shadow: 0 24px 80px rgba(36, 31, 26, 0.12);
    }

    .hero-media figcaption {
        margin-top: 0.8rem;
        font-size: 0.86rem;
        line-height: 1.6;
        color: #675d52;
    }

    .bazu-case-study h1 {
        font-family: "Recia", serif;
    }

    .bazu-case-study :lang(ja) {
        font-family: "Noto Sans JP", sans-serif;
        font-weight: 300;
    }

    .eyebrow {
        margin: 0 0 clamp(1.25rem, 2.5vw, 2rem);
        font-size: clamp(0.72rem, 1.1vw, 0.86rem);
        letter-spacing: 0.32em;
        text-transform: uppercase;
        color: #4e3620;
    }

    h1 {
        margin: 0;
        font-size: clamp(2.75rem, 5.4vw, 4.7rem);
        line-height: 1.08;
        max-width: 13em;
        font-weight: 500;
        text-wrap: balance;
    }

    .lead {
        margin: clamp(1.35rem, 2.4vw, 2rem) 0 0;
        max-width: 62ch;
        font-size: clamp(0.98rem, 1.35vw, 1.16rem);
        line-height: 1.72;
        text-wrap: pretty;
        color: #3d372f;
    }

    .case-study-meta {
        margin-top: 3rem;
        display: grid;
        grid-template-columns: 1fr;
        border-top: 1px solid rgba(78, 54, 32, 0.14);
    }

    .meta-row {
        display: grid;
        grid-template-columns: minmax(8rem, 0.28fr) 1fr;
        gap: clamp(1.5rem, 5vw, 4rem);
        align-items: baseline;
        padding: 1.25rem 0;
        border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(78, 54, 32, 0.14);
    }

    dt {
        margin: 0;
        font-size: 0.78rem;
        font-weight: 700;
        letter-spacing: 0.18em;
        text-transform: uppercase;
        color: #4e3620;
        flex-shrink: 0;
    }

    dd {
        margin: 0;
        font-size: clamp(1rem, 1.4vw, 1.28rem);
        line-height: 1.55;
        color: #1d1a17;
    }

    .case-study-snapshot {
        display: grid;
        grid-template-columns: 1fr;
        gap: 0;
        margin-top: 5rem;
        overflow: hidden;
        border-top: 1px solid rgba(78, 54, 32, 0.16);
        border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(78, 54, 32, 0.16);
    }

    .case-study-snapshot div {
        display: grid;
        grid-template-columns: minmax(7rem, 0.22fr) 1fr;
        gap: clamp(1.25rem, 4vw, 3rem);
        padding: 1.4rem 0;
        border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(78, 54, 32, 0.12);
    }

    .case-study-snapshot div:last-child {
        border-bottom: 0;
    }

    .case-study-snapshot span {
        display: block;
        margin-bottom: 0;
        font-size: 0.76rem;
        font-weight: 700;
        letter-spacing: 0.16em;
        text-transform: uppercase;
        color: #4e3620;
    }

    .case-study-snapshot p {
        margin: 0;
        line-height: 1.75;
        color: #3b352f;
    }

    .case-study-overview,
    .case-study-challenge,
    .case-study-user {
        margin-top: 5rem;
    }

    .case-study-overview h2,
    .case-study-challenge h2,
    .case-study-user h2,
    .case-study-outcome h2 {
        margin: 0 0 2rem;
        font-family: "Space Grotesk", system-ui, sans-serif;
        font-size: 0.78rem;
        font-weight: 700;
        letter-spacing: 0.18em;
        text-transform: uppercase;
        color: #4e3620;
    }

    .case-study-challenge p,
    .case-study-user p {
        max-width: 68ch;
        margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
        color: #3b352f;
        font-size: 1rem;
        line-height: 1.82;
    }

    .case-study-user ul {
        margin: 0 0 1.5rem;
        padding-left: 1.4rem;
        color: #3b352f;
        line-height: 1.8;
    }

    .case-study-user li {
        margin-bottom: 0.9rem;
    }

    .case-study-feature {
        margin-top: 5rem;
    }

    .case-study-feature h2 {
        margin: 0 0 2rem;
        font-family: "Recia", serif;
        font-size: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3.2rem);
        font-weight: 500;
        line-height: 1;
        color: #241f1a;
    }

    .feature-grid {
        display: grid;
        gap: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 4rem);
        align-items: center;
        grid-template-columns: 1.2fr 1fr;
    }

    .feature-grid--reverse {
        grid-template-columns: 1fr 1.2fr;
    }

    .feature-eyebrow {
        margin: 0 0 1rem;
        font-family: "Space Grotesk", system-ui, sans-serif;
        font-size: 0.78rem;
        letter-spacing: 0.18em;
        text-transform: uppercase;
        color: #4e3620;
        font-weight: 700;
    }

    .feature-placeholder {
        min-height: 220px;
        display: grid;
        place-items: center;
        padding: 2rem;
        border: 1px solid rgba(78, 54, 32, 0.18);
        border-radius: 1.5rem;
        color: #4e3620;
        background: rgba(248, 244, 225, 0.46);
        font-style: italic;
        text-align: center;
    }

    .feature-image {
        display: block;
        width: 100%;
        height: auto;
        border-radius: 0.75rem;
        object-fit: cover;
    }

    .machine-visual {
        display: grid;
        place-items: center;
        min-height: 320px;
        padding: 1.5rem;
        overflow: hidden;
        border: 1px solid rgba(78, 54, 32, 0.1);
        border-radius: 0.75rem;
        background: linear-gradient(
            145deg,
            rgba(248, 244, 225, 0.88),
            rgba(229, 220, 207, 0.5)
        );
    }

    .feature-image--machine {
        width: min(100%, 520px);
        border-radius: 0;
        filter: drop-shadow(0 26px 34px rgba(29, 26, 23, 0.22));
    }

    .case-study-visual {
        margin-top: 6rem;
    }

    .case-study-visual h2 {
        margin: 0 0 2.4rem;
        font-family: "Recia", serif;
        font-size: clamp(2.2rem, 5vw, 4.4rem);
        font-weight: 500;
        line-height: 0.98;
        color: #241f1a;
    }

    .visual-grid {
        display: grid;
        gap: clamp(3rem, 7vw, 5.5rem);
        align-items: start;
        grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .visual-copy,
    .type-panel {
        width: 100%;
        max-width: 58rem;
        margin: 0 auto;
    }

    .visual-kicker {
        margin: 0 0 1.15rem;
        color: #4e3620;
        font-size: 0.78rem;
        font-weight: 700;
        letter-spacing: 0.22em;
        line-height: 1.5;
        text-transform: uppercase;
    }

    .visual-lead {
        margin: 0;
        max-width: 52rem;
        color: #2e2923;
        font-family: "Recia", serif;
        font-size: clamp(1.35rem, 2.2vw, 2rem);
        line-height: 1.32;
    }

    .visual-reference {
        margin: 1.5rem 0 0;
        color: #70675d;
        font-size: 0.92rem;
        line-height: 1.7;
    }

    .palette-grid {
        display: grid;
        grid-template-columns: repeat(5, minmax(0, 1fr));
        gap: 0.65rem;
        margin: 2rem 0 0;
    }

    .palette-item {
        min-width: 0;
        padding-top: 0.2rem;
    }

    .palette-chip {
        display: block;
        width: 100%;
        height: clamp(3rem, 7vw, 4.5rem);
        margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
        border: 1px solid rgba(78, 54, 32, 0.12);
        border-radius: 999px 999px 0 0;
    }

    .palette-item strong,
    .palette-item span:last-child {
        display: block;
        overflow-wrap: anywhere;
    }

    .palette-item strong {
        color: #241f1a;
        font-size: 0.82rem;
        font-weight: 600;
        line-height: 1.25;
    }

    .palette-item span:last-child {
        margin-top: 0.25rem;
        color: #82776a;
        font-size: 0.72rem;
        letter-spacing: 0.04em;
    }

    .type-panel {
        padding-top: 0;
    }

    .type-specimen-list {
        display: grid;
        gap: 0;
        border-top: 1px solid rgba(78, 54, 32, 0.14);
    }

    .type-spec {
        display: grid;
        grid-template-columns: minmax(7rem, 0.22fr) minmax(12rem, 0.3fr) 1fr;
        gap: clamp(1.2rem, 3vw, 2.8rem);
        align-items: baseline;
        padding: 1.45rem 0;
        border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(78, 54, 32, 0.14);
    }

    .type-role {
        color: #4e3620;
        font-size: 0.72rem;
        font-weight: 700;
        letter-spacing: 0.18em;
        line-height: 1.45;
        text-transform: uppercase;
    }

    .type-name,
    .type-sample {
        margin: 0;
    }

    .type-name {
        color: #1d1a17;
        font-size: clamp(1.05rem, 1.45vw, 1.24rem);
        line-height: 1.2;
    }

    .type-sample {
        color: #6d6258;
        font-size: 0.92rem;
        line-height: 1.65;
    }

    .type-spec--display .type-name,
    .type-spec--display .type-sample {
        font-family: "Recia", serif;
    }

    .type-spec--display .type-sample {
        color: #241f1a;
        font-size: clamp(1.45rem, 2.4vw, 2.25rem);
        line-height: 1.12;
    }

    .type-spec--functional .type-name,
    .type-spec--functional .type-sample {
        font-family: "Space Grotesk", system-ui, sans-serif;
    }

    .type-spec--japanese .type-name,
    .type-spec--japanese .type-sample {
        font-family: "Noto Sans JP", sans-serif;
        font-weight: 300;
    }

    .case-study-learned {
        margin-top: 5rem;
    }

    .case-study-outcome {
        margin-top: 5rem;
    }

    .outcome-gallery {
        display: grid;
        grid-template-columns: 1.4fr 1fr 1fr;
        gap: 1rem;
        margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
    }

    .outcome-gallery img {
        display: block;
        width: 100%;
        height: 100%;
        min-height: 260px;
        object-fit: cover;
        object-position: top;
        border: 1px solid rgba(78, 54, 32, 0.12);
        border-radius: 1rem;
        background: #f8f4e1;
    }

    .outcome-gallery img:first-child {
        grid-row: span 2;
    }

